+# Commercial licence review — 2026-10-25
+
+**Assessment: the reviewed licences support a commercial, proprietary game.
+No confirmed incompatible licence was identified. Final release clearance still
+requires the remaining notice and provenance checks described below. The scope
+and evidence limits are recorded in this review.**
+
+Scope: the current licence-page registry, recorded asset provenance, native build
+scripts, existing Android dependency notice archives and the retained 5,294-entry
+Android content ZIP. No new app build, device access, deployment or live-service
+mutation was performed. Product sources and media were not changed.
+
+## Findings
+
+### CLR01 — P2: menu music provenance is stale, rather than an unknown third-party grant
+
+`game/soundtrack/audio_world.gd:5` selects the Exploration menu recording. Its Ogg
+is present in the retained export, but `game/assets/audio/menu_exploration_v1/manifest.json:22`
+and `:53` still describe an unknown creator and unreviewed commercial terms.
+The source notice has the same historical limitation.
+
+The owner now confirms that they created this recording with the local WSL
+music-generation model. Read-only inspection identifies the installed application
+as **Magenta RealTime 2, magenta-rt 2.0.3**. Its model card permits Apache-2.0
+code/CC-BY-4.0 weights and states that Google claims no rights in generated
+outputs. The game distributes audio, not the model or its weights. The weight
+licence does not, by itself, place every generated recording under CC BY.
+[Model terms](https://github.com/magenta/magenta-realtime/blob/main/MODEL.md).
+
+**Action:** update the recording's provenance/notice with the owner's authorship,
+identified model and output terms. Retain the original MP3 hash. The review did
+not locate an output-side manifest linking the exact MP3 to a generation run,
+so the specific file-to-model attribution relies on the owner's clarification
+and the identified installation, rather than a recovered generation receipt.
+No replacement of the recording is required merely because it was AI-generated.
+
+### CLR02 — P2: wet-glass provenance should record the clarified ChatGPT origin
+
+`licenses/ASSETS.md:175` records adaptation of an owner-supplied shader attachment,
+but does not identify the upstream permission. The owner now identifies the
+source as a ChatGPT web session. The current runtime shader samples an offline
+bake generated by `game/tests/bake_storm_glass.gdshader`; the baked texture is
+exported. Excluding the bake script alone would not resolve source rights.
+
+OpenAI's consumer and business terms assign its rights, if any, in outputs to
+the user/customer, subject to applicable law. Those terms support commercial
+use; they do not guarantee exclusivity, copyright protection or clearance of
+third-party material. No specific third-party shader licence was identified.
+[Europe terms](https://openai.com/policies/eu-terms-of-use/),
+[business agreement §4](https://openai.com/policies/services-agreement/).
+
+**Action:** record the owner-supplied ChatGPT origin and retain the original
+conversation/code if available. This clarification resolves the earlier
+assumption of an unidentified external shader source; it is not evidence that
+every possible third-party right has been independently cleared.
+
+### CLR03 — P2: final Android native-runtime notice coverage remains unverified
+
+The reader includes actual AndroidX and Google Identity notice texts and
+debug-only Mobile Ads notices. These are appropriate sources, but the reviewed
+archive is a Godot **content ZIP**, not the final Gradle-produced APK/AAB.
+
+`scripts/build_track_geometry.ps1:33` statically links the Android C++ runtime.
+Read-only ELF inspection finds NDK C++ symbols and dependencies on Android system
+libraries, with no `libc++_shared.so` dependency. The custom native notice exposed
+by `game/legal/third_party_notices.gd:15` currently contains godot-cpp MIT only.
+The installed NDK contains additional LLVM/libc++ licence material that is not
+identified by that notice. LLVM licences permit commercial use and include
+object-code exceptions, so this is **not** evidence of a noncommercial licence
+or a requirement to publish the game source.
+[LLVM licence and exceptions](https://github.com/llvm/llvm-project/blob/main/libcxx/LICENSE.TXT).
+
+**Action:** reconcile the actual release dependency/native-library inventory with
+the displayed notices. Include applicable NDK runtime notices, or document the
+precise exception relied upon, and retain any remaining third-party notices.
+Do not infer completeness from the three top-level dependency archives alone.
+[Google's notice guidance](https://developers.google.com/android/guides/opensource).
+
+## Commercial compatibility matrix
+
+| Component/licence | Commercial use | Conditions relevant to this app |
+|---|---|---|
+| Godot Engine, godot-cpp, flag-icons — MIT | Yes, including a proprietary game | Retain copyright, permission and disclaimer notices; retain engine-library notices. [Godot](https://godotengine.org/license/) |
+| AndroidX and Apache-2.0 components | Yes | Include the licence and applicable NOTICE material; preserve required change/copyright notices. This does not require publishing our independent game code. [Apache 2.0](https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0) |
+| Barlow, Libre Baskerville, Noto JP/KR, Google Sans — OFL 1.1 | Yes, bundled in a paid/ad-supported app | Preserve font copyright/OFL; do not sell the fonts alone. Modified fonts must meet reserved-name requirements. The inspected source fonts are recorded as unmodified. [OFL](https://openfontlicense.org/open-font-license-official-text/) |
+| Recorded tyre squeal — CC BY 3.0 | Yes | Preserve creator/title/source/licence credit and identify edits. The current page does this. Preserve recipients' CC rights; do not apply additional restrictions/effective DRM to the CC material. [Source](https://opengameart.org/content/car-tire-squeal-skid-loop), [terms §4](https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0/legalcode) |
+| Nox, VSCO CE, Karoryfer and other documented CC0 recordings | Yes | Copyright attribution is generally optional; retain source evidence. CC0 does not clear unrelated trademark/privacy rights. [Nox](https://nox-sound-design.itch.io/essentials-series-sfx-nox-sound), [VSCO pinned licence](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sgossner/VSCO-2-CE/440300901dfe9275fd84e0b7763af1f8443ae62e/LICENSE) |
+| Pixabay rain/wind/thunder/crash/grass | Yes, incorporated into the game | No standalone stock/audio resale or false ownership/endorsement. Credit is optional. Public listing identity and retained local-source evidence matter. [Pixabay §5–6](https://pixabay.com/service/terms/) |
+| Magenta-generated music | Compatible with the reviewed output terms | The model provider claims no output rights. Preserve original generation provenance and rights in any supplied conditioning/samples. Do not confuse model redistribution terms with output terms. [Model card](https://github.com/magenta/magenta-realtime/blob/main/MODEL.md) |
+| ChatGPT code and OpenAI-generated artwork | Compatible with provider output ownership terms | The applicable account terms and rights in input/reference material still matter. Generated outputs are not promised to be unique or independently non-infringing. [EU terms](https://openai.com/policies/eu-terms-of-use/), [business terms](https://openai.com/policies/services-agreement/) |
+| Windows GCC runtime with Runtime Library Exception; MinGW/winpthreads | Yes, with applicable conditions | The exception permits proprietary target code from an eligible compilation process. Keep the supplied notices; separately redistributing a GPL runtime is a different case. [GNU exception guidance](https://www.gnu.org/licenses/exceptions.html) |
+| Google Identity/AdMob SDKs and Google sign-in artwork | Commercial apps are supported, subject to service terms | SDK/service policies and notices apply. The Google button/logo is for the sign-in action, not general game branding. AdMob is currently debug-only. [API terms](https://developers.google.com/terms), [branding](https://developers.google.com/identity/branding-guidelines), [Ads terms](https://developers.google.com/admob/terms) |
+
+The current terms draft explicitly preserves applicable third-party/open-source
+rights. Retain that carve-out in the published version, particularly for CC BY
+audio and OFL fonts. Ordinary file compression/packing is not automatically DRM;
+check any later asset encryption or store-imposed restrictions separately.
+[Creative Commons FAQ](https://creativecommons.org/faq/).
+
+Original code-authored vehicle/scenery assets have project provenance. Reference
+photos, manufacturer branding and legacy Slicks fixtures are not licensed merely
+because they were supplied as references. The retained ZIP has no legacy/Slicks
+filename matches and excludes test fixtures; filename inspection alone does not
+prove the origin of every geometric layout. This review does not replace a
+visual trademark/design-rights review or a creator-track rights process.
+
+The hosted backend is separate from app distribution. Its name-filter dataset
+has a retained Shutterstock CC BY 4.0 notice; that licence permits commercial
+use, with attribution when shared. This review is not a complete audit of all
+server wheels/container dependencies or a privacy/store-compliance approval.
+
+## Evidence and actual checks
+
+- Inspected the retained content ZIP: **5,294 entries**; active menu music and
+  wet-glass baked data are included. Android plugin/native binaries are packaged
+  separately, so final APK/AAB completeness is not claimed.
+- `python scripts/check_audio_licenses.py --require-originals --output docs/evidence/commercial-licence-review-2026-10-25/weather-validation.json`:
+  **76 checks, zero failures; four originals, eight masters, seven encodings**.
+- Read the local SDK notice archives and checked GPL/NonCommercial text matches
+  in context. Such words appear within broad J2ObjC/Kotlin licence bundles;
+  a keyword hit alone does not establish a prohibited dependency or application
+  copyleft obligation.
+- Read the identified WSL installation's README and verification metadata:
+  Magenta RT2 / magenta-rt 2.0.3. No model loaded, generation run, software
+  installed, network request made from WSL, or owner process restarted.
+- Inspected the Android native build flags and ELF dynamic dependencies/symbols.
+  The `Select-Object -First` symbol-preview pipeline returned exit 1 after its
+  requested five lines; the ELF dependency inspection itself produced the four
+  system-library dependencies. No native binary was executed or changed.
+- Verified current primary terms for MIT/Godot, OFL, CC BY/CC0, Pixabay,
+  Magenta, OpenAI, Google SDK notices/branding and GCC/LLVM exceptions.
+
+Read-only review evidence and input hashes are in
+`docs/evidence/commercial-licence-review-2026-10-25/`. No runtime code, media,
+licence-page text or historical manifests were changed by this review.
